1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,029
Welcome.

2
00:00:01,029 --> 00:00:05,594
This course is NVIDIA's Getting Started With Isaac Sim learning path,

3
00:00:05,594 --> 00:00:08,969
rewritten step by step for Isaac Sim six point one.

4
00:00:08,969 --> 00:00:12,938
The original course was written for version four point five,

5
00:00:12,938 --> 00:00:16,577
so many menus, sensors and Python imports have changed.

6
00:00:16,577 --> 00:00:23,723
Every change is marked in the lessons, and every lesson comes with a checkpoint script you can run yourself.

7
00:00:24,623 --> 00:00:26,607
The course has five modules.

8
00:00:26,607 --> 00:00:32,347
In module one you build a small robot from scratch and stream its lidar to ROS 2.

9
00:00:32,347 --> 00:00:36,457
Module two imports a real robot, Carter, from a URDF file.

10
00:00:36,457 --> 00:00:40,638
Module three generates a synthetic dataset with Replicator.

11
00:00:40,638 --> 00:00:44,890
Module four closes the loop with ROS 2 software in the loop,

12
00:00:44,890 --> 00:00:51,268
and module five explains how the same setup connects to a Jetson for hardware in the loop.

13
00:00:52,168 --> 00:00:54,424
Here is the routine for every lesson.

14
00:00:54,424 --> 00:00:56,132
First, read the lesson file.

15
00:00:56,132 --> 00:01:00,219
It keeps the course structure and marks every six point one change.

16
00:01:00,219 --> 00:01:03,329
Then do the steps yourself in the Isaac Sim window.

17
00:01:03,329 --> 00:01:06,196
You learn the interface by clicking through it.

18
00:01:06,196 --> 00:01:09,429
If you get stuck, run the matching checkpoint script.

19
00:01:09,429 --> 00:01:12,478
It builds the finished result, so you can compare.

20
00:01:12,478 --> 00:01:18,578
And every script has a headless test mode that prints pass or fail, which is handy after an upgrade.

21
00:01:19,478 --> 00:01:21,422
Four changes matter most.

22
00:01:21,422 --> 00:01:24,765
The RTX lidar replaces the old PhysX lidar.

23
00:01:24,765 --> 00:01:29,587
The URDF importer was rewritten and now needs two extra steps.

24
00:01:29,587 --> 00:01:36,585
ROS 2 Jazzy libraries ship inside Isaac Sim, so you no longer source ROS before launching.

25
00:01:36,585 --> 00:01:41,095
And the old omni dot isaac dot core Python module is gone.

26
00:01:41,095 --> 00:01:44,128
The cheat sheet file lists all of this.

27
00:01:44,128 --> 00:01:46,305
Let's start with module one.

